  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Recipes tab of the tool library window now has two inputs for each material row, under the table:\n\n- **Surface speed** (Vc, m/min; sfm in an inch document).\n- **Chip load** (fz, mm per tooth; inch in an inch document).\n\nA Vc edit sets the stored spindle rpm of the row: n = Vc x 1000 / (pi x D). An fz edit sets the stored feed of the row: F = fz x z x n. The rpm stays. The table shows the new rpm or feed immediately, and the inputs show the values that follow from the table. The derived line of #4337 is now the hover text of the two inputs.\n\n- The stored values do not change. The project file does not change.\n- The edits write the draft of the window only. The one Apply of the editor lands them as one `ChangeTool`, one undo step. No command is new, so no MCP tool is necessary.\n- The chip load input is disabled when the tool has no flute count, or when the row has no rpm. The surface speed input is disabled when the tool diameter is not above zero. The disabled input gives the reason in its hover text. The conversion functions return the reason as an error, so nothing divides by zero.\n\nThe change stays in the Recipes tab code (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_library_dialog/`). The shared cutting table (`tool_cutting_rows.rs`) does not change. The decision is in `docs/decisions/4453-recipe-fz-vc-inputs.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_recipe_speeds::an_fz_or_vc_edit_sets_the_stored_feed_or_rpm_and_is_one_undo_step`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_recipe_speeds::a_missing_flute_count_or_a_zero_diameter_refuses_the_input`\n- `egui_app::tool_library_dialog::recipes_speeds::tests::*` (four unit tests: fz to F and back, Vc to rpm and back, the refusals, the inch lens)\n- Updated: `tool_library_recipes::the_document_material_row_is_marked` (reads the Vc input), `tool_library_recipes::the_derived_line_follows_rpm_and_feed` (reads the cached line), `page_layout_tool_library::layout_window_tool_editor` (the inputs stand under the table, above the buttons, Vc left of fz).\n\n`#[test]` count of `crates/ui`: 2009 before, 2015 after (+6).\n\nThe new file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_recipe_speeds.rs` is a module of the `camcraft-ui` lib tests (one sorted `mod` line), not a new test binary.\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main && cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` on head `53c9072f0` (winbuild lane): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The `ui suites: lib` step holds the pinning tests. Clippy is clean.\n\nThe first run on `c54f012e5` was red: clippy found two collapsible `if` statements, and the refusal test used `Harness::run` while a press on a disabled field drags the window. Both are fixed on the branch.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Typed input (keyboard) into the two fields. The tests drag the fields.\n- The inch lens in the UI test. The unit test covers the conversion.\n- Light lane and example catalog: the diff is UI only and changes no post and no toolpath.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (main): the surface speed and the chip load are a read-only line under the table.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4459/before.png)\n\nAfter: each row has a surface speed input and a chip load input. The derived line is their hover text.\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4459/after.png)\n\nChangelog: The Recipes tab edits the surface speed and the chip load of each row; the rpm or the feed follows.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4453\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
